controls=[
('Define the bounded outcome','Write the exact coordination outcome and list decisions reserved for workforce, employment, pay, safety, legal, privacy, security, client, and vendor owners. A support specialist may assemble and compare evidence, but pressure to fill coverage never becomes implied authority.'),
('Authenticate the intake','Assign a stable case key and verify the requester, worker or work item, assignment, effective period, location or time zone, and approved channel. Preserve the original instruction and label missing fields unknown rather than copying a value from a similar worker.'),
('Rank the sources','Name the controlling roster, schedule, work order, access record, custody record, worker notice, or owner instruction for every consequential value. Keep observation time and version beside the value so a later correction does not erase what informed the action.'),
('Separate preparation from decisions','Record source checking, proposed coordination, owner review, approval, execution, communication, and verification as different states. A complete packet is not a staffing decision, and a sent message is not evidence that access, schedule, payroll, or custody changed.'),
('Use least privilege','Give each participant only the fields and actions needed for the assigned step. Use named accounts, multifactor authentication, restricted exports, reviewable access changes, and time-bounded permissions. Never share credentials to avoid a delayed owner response.'),
('Handle exceptions explicitly','Use distinct reason codes for missing source, identity mismatch, conflicting instruction, stale evidence, duplicate candidate, unavailable owner, system outage, safety concern, privacy review, and scope change. Every exception needs an owner, next-check time, and safe stop.'),
('Review before execution','A second reviewer should reconstruct the identity, source, authority, proposed action, and remaining uncertainty. Test effective dates and destination identifiers. Return an unclear record rather than allowing a persuasive summary to substitute for verifiable evidence.'),
('Confirm the handoff','State what changed, what did not change, which version was used, who now owns the decision, and when acknowledgement is due. Capture a receipt or destination state. Silence and send status do not prove that a consequential handoff succeeded.'),
('Protect personal information','Keep control references in the coordination queue and sensitive worker, health, safety, identity, financial, or employment material in approved systems. Apply purpose limitation, controlled exports, retention dates, and disposal evidence to temporary working copies.'),
('Prepare for outages','Issue temporary identifiers from a controlled sequence, restrict local storage, log actions and timestamps, and prohibit irreversible execution unless an approved emergency rule permits it. Reconcile every temporary item to primary-system events after service returns.'),
('Measure quality','Reconcile opening cases, additions, transfers, approved completions, withdrawals, reopened work, and ending cases. Show exception reasons and age bands beside throughput, separating coordinator time, owner wait, system delay, destination failure, and correction rework.'),
('Close with evidence','Completion requires current sources, necessary approval, executed destination state, communication receipt, residual limitation, and explicit next ownership. Reopen after a material policy, system, schedule, assignment, identity, or scope change.'),
]
research_controls=[
('Research question','Define one bounded operational question and distinguish observed process evidence from workforce, legal, safety, employment, pay, vendor, or client outcomes.'),
('Population and observation window','Freeze the eligible population, systems, dates, time zone, and inclusion and exclusion rules before viewing results. Reconcile opening units, additions, withdrawals, resolutions, and unresolved ending units.'),
('Unit of analysis','Choose whether a unit is a worker, shift, request, work order, assignment, source event, destination, or correction episode. Do not count linked events as independent successes.'),
('Data dictionary','Record pseudonymous key, source class, timestamp, eligibility, status, owner, pause reason, destination evidence, reviewer, and adjudication. Blank, unavailable, and confirmed negative states require different codes.'),
('Collection protocol','Collect on a fixed cadence, preserve source versions, and distinguish scheduled observations from incident-triggered reviews. Document deviations and never bypass access controls to improve apparent completeness.'),
('Reviewer independence','Train reviewers outside the analytic sample and preserve their first classifications before discussion. Separate disagreement about facts, authority, severity, and missing evidence.'),
('Primary measures','Lock numerator, denominator, start and stop events, pause treatment, withdrawal handling, and censoring before calculation. Publish counts beside rates, medians beside ranges, and unresolved cases beside closed cases.'),
('Quality controls','Check identifiers, timestamps, impossible sequences, duplicate records, missing destinations, and edits after observation. Automation finds inconsistencies but cannot make workforce judgments.'),
('Sensitivity analysis','Repeat measures under reasonable alternate cutoffs, pause rules, and missing-evidence treatments. Exclude incident-triggered reviews separately and disclose when extreme cases drive a conclusion.'),
('Privacy and security','Collect minimum necessary fields, restrict exports and identity crosswalks, log access, and define disposal dates before collection. Aggregate results so worker narratives cannot be reconstructed.'),
('Limitations','Systems may lag, unrecorded coordination may exist, and policy, demand, staffing mix, owner availability, and case difficulty can change together. Association cannot establish intent or causation.'),
('Governance and stopping','Name protocol, data, operational, privacy, safety, and remediation owners. Pause on unauthorized disclosure, unsafe access, action without approval, corrupted sources, or loss of the promised boundary.'),
('Operational interpretation','Convert findings into better evidence fields, recheck intervals, ownership maps, and testable exception routes rather than worker, vendor, or provider rankings. Verify changes with fresh cases.'),
('Transparent reporting','Publish case flow, denominators, exclusions, unresolved cases, observation coverage, deviations, sensitivity results, and limitations together, keeping claims within the tested population, systems, and period.'),
]

